Package: libgeist0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: library for reading IBM BookManager BOO books
 libgeist parses an IBM BookManager BOO container and renders its topics to
 Markdown or HTML. It is self-contained: it decides nothing about
 presentation, and a consumer supplies the link resolvers, the page chrome
 and the URL space it wants.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libgeist-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libgeist0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: library for reading IBM BookManager BOO books - development files
 libgeist parses an IBM BookManager BOO container and renders its topics to
 Markdown or HTML.
 .
 This package contains the headers and the CMake package configuration
 needed to build against libgeist, and the static library: geist_static is
 part of the exported CMake target set, so omitting it would leave
 find_package(geist) describing a target whose file is not installed.

Package: geist-tools
Section: utils
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: command-line tools for IBM BookManager BOO books
 Tools for inspecting and converting BOO books:
 .
  * booinfo   - book metadata
  * bootoc    - table of contents
  * boorsrc   - list and extract stored images
  * boorender - render a topic to Markdown or HTML
  * bootrace  - trace rendered output back to the source bytes
  * boo2git   - export a whole book to a folder tree

Package: geist-reader
Section: text
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: desktop reader for IBM BookManager BOO books
 The Geist Hardcopy Reader, a Qt6 desktop reader laid out after IBM's
 BookManager SoftCopy Reader: a topic tree, a divider and a topic pane, with
 separate font-size controls for each.

Package: libapache2-mod-geist
Section: httpd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, apache2
Description: Apache module serving IBM BookManager BOO books
 mod_geist serves a BOO book over HTTP. A book is addressed by its own path,
 so a book in the document root is browsable without any registration or
 conversion step, and its topics, stored images and the file itself hang
 below that path.
 .
 With BooIndex enabled a directory of books lists itself, after BookManager
 BookServer's bookshelf page.
